SUMMARY:Milky Way · Norah Head Lighthouse · Core rising beside the lighth
 ouse
LOCATION:Norah Head Rock Pool\, Bald Street\, Norah Head NSW 2263
GEO:-33.27893;151.56964
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.27893,151.56964
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The galactic core rising out of the Pacific beside Norah 
 Head Lighthouse. Early season\, so the core is low and short lived before 
 dawn. Frame the lighthouse low and let the core climb beside it.\nPriority
 : Optional\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nNight of Sat 06 Feb into Sun 07 Feb 2027
 .\nShoot window: 02:55 to 04:45 (core between 8° and 60° high\, sky full
 y dark\, moon down).\nBest composition: about 04:45\, core 29° high in th
 e ESE.\nArrive by 02:10 to set up and focus.\nSunset 19:54 · astronomical
  dusk 21:25 · astronomical dawn 04:49 · sunrise 06:21\nMoon: new moon Su
 n 07 Feb 02:56. 0% lit and below the horizon during the window. Moonrise S
 un 06:35 · Moonset Sat 19:40\n\nCORE POSITION\n03:00  altitude 9°\, azim
 uth 119° ESE\n03:30  altitude 15°\, azimuth 115° ESE\n04:00  altitude 2
 1°\, azimuth 112° ESE\n04:30  altitude 26°\, azimuth 109° ESE\n\nTIDES
  (BOM prediction\, Newcastle)\nNewcastle is the nearest BOM standard port.
  Treat times as approximate for this site.\nLow water Sun 03:13  0.58 m\nA
 t the best composition (04:45): about 0.75 m and rising.\nPredictions excl
 ude swell\, wind setup and wave run up. Check BOM coastal waters and swell
  forecasts on the day.\nSource table: https://www.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/
 IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP004.pdf\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nNorah Head Rock Pool\, Bal
 d Street\, Norah Head NSW 2263\nCamera pin: https://www.google.com/maps/se
 arch/?api=1&query=-33.27893\,151.56964\nSubject pin (Norah Head Lighthouse
 ): https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.28165\,151.57635\nN
 orah Head Lighthouse is 693 m away on bearing 116° (ESE). At 04:45 the co
 re is 9 degrees left of it\, 29° up. To stack the core straight above it\
 , move about 104 m to your right\, keeping the same distance.\nStraight li
 ne from Neutral Bay: about 70 km.\n\nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\n
 FE 12-24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm for single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II fo
 r a sharper multi row panorama.\n12 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm
 : up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 mm f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForegr
 ound: separate longer frames at ISO 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from
  the same tripod position.\nPeak Design travel tripod\, red head torch\, d
 ew heater strap on the lens.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Work from the public rock p
 latform and foreshore\, not the lighthouse grounds.\n- Rock platform: chec
 k swell and tide first. Wet rock is slippery in the dark.\n- Light from th
 e lighthouse beam sweeps the frame. Time exposures between passes or blend
 .\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pin and time set)
 : https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-33.27893\,151.56964&center=-33.27893
 \,151.56964&z=15&dt=2027-02-06T17%3A45%3A00.000Z&sll=-33.28165\,151.57635&
 fovb=115.9&fovhfov=104.10&fovvfov=81.20&fovd=693&fovo=l&fovov=1\nPhotoPill
 s: Planner > drop the pin at the camera coordinates > set the date and tim
 e above > Milky Way layer. Use Night AR on site to confirm the core path.\
 nCheck cloud (BOM and Windy) and light pollution (lightpollutionmap.info) 
 two days out.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phases: US Naval Observatory 2027 table (aa
 .usno.navy.mil).\nSun\, moon and core positions: computed with Skyfield an
 d JPL DE421 for the camera pin.\nCoordinates: OpenStreetMap. Terrain horiz
 ons: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.\nTide predictions: Bureau of Meteorology 
 2027 tide tables\, Copyright Commonwealth of Australia 2026. Based on Bure
 au of Meteorology information that has been modified. The Bureau does not 
 necessarily support or endorse\, or have any connection with\, this produc
 t\, and gives no warranty about the information. Full terms: page 4 of the
  source PDF.
CATEGORIES:Astrophotography
