SUMMARY:Deep Sky · Gary Phayes 1 on 1 workshop · Learn the Esprit 80ED ri
 g (booked)
LOCATION:Blue Mountains\, Blackheath area NSW 2785 (meeting point TBC with 
 Gary)
GEO:-33.63389;150.28472
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-33.63389,150.28472
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: One on one deep sky workshop with Gary Phayes on your own
  rig: setup\, polar alignment\, focusing with the EAF\, plate solving and 
 capture with the ASI2600MC Air\, then stacking and processing basics. Book
 ed. Weather reschedule agreed with Gary.\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nThursday 1
 1 February 2027\, about 18:00 to 01:00  (work day)\nSunset 19:55 · astron
 omical dusk 21:26 · Moonset 21:58.\nMoon: new moon Sun 07 Feb 02:56. Waxi
 ng crescent\, 21% lit at astronomical dusk and setting early\, so the even
 ing sky goes dark quickly.\n\nTARGET ALTITUDES (Blackheath\, altitude and 
 direction)\nOrion Nebula (M42): 21:30 61° N · 23:30 47° WNW · 01:30 24
 ° W\nRosette Nebula (NGC 2237): 21:30 50° NNE · 23:30 47° NNW · 01:30
  29° WNW\nTarantula Nebula (NGC 2070): 21:30 54° S · 23:30 50° SSW · 
 01:30 40° SSW\nCarina Nebula (NGC 3372): 21:30 37° SE · 23:30 52° SSE 
 · 01:30 62° SSE\n\nWHERE\nBlue Mountains\, Blackheath area NSW 2785 (mee
 ting point TBC with Gary)\nPlaceholder pin: https://www.google.com/maps/se
 arch/?api=1&query=-33.63389\,150.28472\n\nBRING YOUR RIG\n- Sky-Watcher Es
 prit 80ED Pro on the ZWO AM5N mount\n- ZWO ASI2600MC Air (built in ASIAIR)
  with the ZWO EAF focuser\n- Antlia Triband II RGB Ultra 2 inch in the ZWO
  filter drawer\n- PrimaLuceLab dew heater and the ZWO DC Y splitter cable\
 n- Laptop for stacking\, head torch\, warm layers\, gloves and a beanie\n\
 nPREP (reminder fires 7 days before)\n- Update ASIAIR app and camera\, mou
 nt and EAF firmware at home\, not in the field.\n- Charge or check power f
 or the mount\, camera and dew heaters for about 7 hours.\n- Dry run assemb
 ly and balance at home\, and write down every cable run.\n- Confirm the me
 eting point and start time with Gary.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Thursday\, a work 
 day. The Blackheath area is roughly 2 h by car from North Sydney. Leave by
  about 15:45\, or take the afternoon off.\n- Times are approximate per Gar
 y: about 6 pm to 1 am.\n- Gary's site lists Blue Mountains field locations
  and his Pulpit Rock Gallery training room. The pin is Blackheath town unt
 il he confirms the meeting point.\n- Night temperature at about 1\,000 m c
 an be cool even in February. Pack layers.\n\nSOURCES\nDate and times: emai
 l thread with Gary Phayes\, October 2026.\nLocation area: garyphayes.photo
 graphy/deep-sky-moon-planets.\nSun\, moon and target positions: computed w
 ith Skyfield and JPL DE421.
CATEGORIES:Astrophotography
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
