SUMMARY:Milky Way · Little Blowhole · Core rising over the Little Blowhol
 e rock platform
LOCATION:Little Blowhole\, off Tingira Crescent\, Kiama NSW 2533
GEO:-34.68671;150.85915
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-34.68671,150.85915
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The core rising out of the Pacific above the dark volcani
 c rock platform and the Little Blowhole. Pairs with Cathedral Rocks the ne
 xt night for one Kiama weekend.\nPriority: Optional\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\
 nNight of Fri 05 Mar into Sat 06 Mar 2027.\nShoot window: 01:10 to 03:00 (
 core between 8° and 60° high\, sky fully dark\, moon down\, low tide).\n
 Rock platform shoot: the window is cut to low tide plus or minus 90 minute
 s.\nBest composition: about 03:00\, core 29° high in the ESE.\nArrive by 
 00:25 to set up and focus.\nSunset 19:29 · astronomical dusk 20:55 · ast
 ronomical dawn 05:21 · sunrise 06:47\nMoon: new moon Mon 08 Mar 20:29. 7%
  lit and below the horizon during the window. Moonrise Sat 04:26 · Moonse
 t Fri 17:47\n\nCORE POSITION\n01:30  altitude 12°\, azimuth 117° ESE\n02
 :00  altitude 18°\, azimuth 113° ESE\n02:30  altitude 23°\, azimuth 110
 ° ESE\n03:00  altitude 29°\, azimuth 107° ESE\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\
 , Port Kembla)\nPort Kembla is the nearest BOM standard port. Treat times 
 as approximate for this site.\nThe window above is cut to low tide 01:33 (
 0.57 m) plus or minus 90 minutes.\nLow water Sat 01:33  0.57 m\nAt the bes
 t composition (03:00): about 0.70 m and rising.\nPredictions exclude swell
 \, wind setup and wave run up. Check BOM coastal waters and swell forecast
 s on the day.\nSource table: https://www.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_
 2027_NSW_TP006.pdf\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nLittle Blowhole\, off Tingira Cresc
 ent\, Kiama NSW 2533\nCamera pin: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=
 1&query=-34.68671\,150.85915\nFace ESE (azimuth 107°) at 03:00.\nStraight
  line from Neutral Bay: about 100 km.\n\nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A
 1)\nFE 12-24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm for single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM I
 I for a sharper multi row panorama.\n12 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 1
 4 mm: up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 mm f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nFo
 reground: separate longer frames at ISO 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames 
 from the same tripod position.\nPeak Design travel tripod\, red head torch
 \, dew heater strap on the lens.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Access: car park and lo
 okout off Tingira Crescent\, about 2 km south of Kiama town. The site is a
  little hard to find\, so check it in daylight.\n- Official listing: free 
 entry\, car park\, lookouts. Not suitable for people with access needs.\n-
  The blowhole fires best with a north east swell. That same swell makes th
 e platform dangerous. Shoot from the lookout if waves reach the rocks.\n- 
 Clear ocean horizon to the ESE. No terrain above 1 degree.\n\nVERIFY BEFOR
 E YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pin and time set): https://app.pho
 toephemeris.com/?ll=-34.68671\,150.85915&center=-34.68671\,150.85915&z=15&
 dt=2027-03-05T16%3A00%3A00.000Z\nPhotoPills: Planner > drop the pin at the
  camera coordinates > set the date and time above > Milky Way layer. Use N
 ight AR on site to confirm the core path.\nCheck cloud (BOM and Windy) and
  light pollution (lightpollutionmap.info) two days out.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon p
 hases: US Naval Observatory 2027 table (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nSun\, moon and
  core positions: computed with Skyfield and JPL DE421 for the camera pin.\
 nCoordinates: OpenStreetMap. Terrain horizons: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.
 \nTide predictions: Bureau of Meteorology 2027 tide tables\, Copyright Com
 monwealth of Australia 2026. Based on Bureau of Meteorology information th
 at has been modified. The Bureau does not necessarily support or endorse\,
  or have any connection with\, this product\, and gives no warranty about 
 the information. Full terms: page 4 of the source PDF.
