SUMMARY:Milky Way · Cathedral Rocks · Core over the rock stacks and throu
 gh the sea cave
LOCATION:Cliff Drive viewpoint above Cathedral Rocks\, Kiama Downs NSW 2533
GEO:-34.64444;150.85547
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-34.64444,150.85547
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: Two compositions. First\, the core framed by the sea cave
  in the cliff\, looking out to the main sea stack\, while the tide is low.
  Second\, the core rising over the Cathedral Rocks sea stacks from the cli
 ff top\, which works all night.\nPriority: High\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nNig
 ht of Sat 06 Mar into Sun 07 Mar 2027.\nShoot window: 01:03 to 05:18 (core
  between 8° and 60° high\, sky fully dark\, moon down).\nBest compositio
 n: about 02:58\, core 30° high in the ESE.\nArrive by 00:18 to set up and
  focus.\nSunset 19:27 · astronomical dusk 20:53 · astronomical dawn 05:2
 2 · sunrise 06:48\nMoon: new moon Mon 08 Mar 20:29. 3% lit and below the 
 horizon during the window. Moonrise Sun 05:25 · Moonset Sat 18:16\n\nCORE
  POSITION\n01:30  altitude 13°\, azimuth 117° ESE\n02:00  altitude 19°\
 , azimuth 113° ESE\n02:30  altitude 24°\, azimuth 110° ESE\n03:00  alti
 tude 30°\, azimuth 106° ESE\n03:30  altitude 36°\, azimuth 103° ESE\n0
 4:00  altitude 42°\, azimuth 100° E\n04:30  altitude 48°\, azimuth 96°
  E\n05:00  altitude 55°\, azimuth 93° E\n\nSEA CAVE WINDOW (Cathedral Ro
 cks sea cave)\n01:03 to 03:38: low tide 02:13 (0.52 m) plus or minus 90 mi
 nutes\, inside the dark sky window.\nCore 8° high at 120° ESE at the sta
 rt\, 38° at 102° at the end.\nBe out of the cave by 03:38. Then shoot th
 e stacks from the cliff top until 05:18.\nAccess pin: https://www.google.c
 om/maps/search/?api=1&query=-34.63931\,150.85258 (Parking opposite Moona A
 venue\, North Kiama Drive\, Kiama Downs NSW 2533)\nSEA CAVE SAFETY: scout 
 the cave\, the approach and your exit in daylight on an earlier visit.\nOn
 ly go in on a falling or low tide with small swell. Leave the cave by the 
 time shown\, whatever the shot.\nNever go alone. Carry a phone in a dry ba
 g and a spare head torch. Watch every set of waves.\n\nTIDES (BOM predicti
 on\, Port Kembla)\nPort Kembla is the nearest BOM standard port. Treat tim
 es as approximate for this site.\nLow water Sun 02:13  0.52 m\nHigh water 
 Sun 08:35  1.66 m\nAt the best composition (02:58): about 0.56 m and risin
 g.\nPredictions exclude swell\, wind setup and wave run up. Check BOM coas
 tal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nSource table: https://www.bom.
 gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP006.pdf\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nCliff 
 Drive viewpoint above Cathedral Rocks\, Kiama Downs NSW 2533\nCamera pin: 
 https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-34.64444\,150.85547\nSubj
 ect pin (Cathedral Rocks sea stacks): https://www.google.com/maps/search/?
 api=1&query=-34.64481\,150.85670\nCathedral Rocks sea stacks is 120 m away
  on bearing 110° (ESE). At 02:58 the core is 4 degrees left of it\, 30° 
 up. To stack the core straight above it\, move about 8 m to your right\, k
 eeping the same distance.\nStraight line from Neutral Bay: about 96 km.\n\
 nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\nFE 12-24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm fo
 r single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II for a sharper multi row panorama.\n12 
 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm: up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 m
 m f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForeground: separate longer frames at ISO 
 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from the same tripod position.\nPeak Des
 ign travel tripod\, red head torch\, dew heater strap on the lens.\n\nFIEL
 D NOTES\n- Access: park opposite Moona Avenue on North Kiama Drive\, take 
 a path down to Jones Beach\, turn right and walk to the headland.\n- The c
 ave sits in the cliff with a framed view of a main sea stack. Its exact sp
 ot and mouth direction are not mapped\, so drop your own pin on the daylig
 ht scout and check the core line with PhotoPills Night AR.\n- The cliff to
 p viewpoint needs no tide. Move up there once the cave window closes.\n- L
 ong exposure smooths the surf around the stacks. Shoot the foreground at b
 lue hour if possible.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subje
 ct pin and time set): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-34.64444\,150.85
 547&center=-34.64444\,150.85547&z=15&dt=2027-03-06T15%3A58%3A00.000Z&sll=-
 34.64481\,150.85670&fovb=110.1&fovhfov=104.10&fovvfov=81.20&fovd=120&fovo=
 l&fovov=1\nPhotoPills: Planner > drop the pin at the camera coordinates > 
 set the date and time above > Milky Way layer. Use Night AR on site to con
 firm the core path.\nCheck cloud (BOM and Windy) and light pollution (ligh
 tpollutionmap.info) two days out.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phases: US Naval Observ
 atory 2027 table (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nSun\, moon and core positions: compu
 ted with Skyfield and JPL DE421 for the camera pin.\nCoordinates: OpenStre
 etMap. Terrain horizons: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.\nTide predictions: Bu
 reau of Meteorology 2027 tide tables\, Copyright Commonwealth of Australia
  2026. Based on Bureau of Meteorology information that has been modified. 
 The Bureau does not necessarily support or endorse\, or have any connectio
 n with\, this product\, and gives no warranty about the information. Full 
 terms: page 4 of the source PDF.
