SUMMARY:Milky Way · Bogey Hole · Core over the convict cut ocean pool
LOCATION:The Bogey Hole\, below King Edward Park\, York Drive\, Newcastle N
 SW 2300
GEO:-32.93522;151.78164
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-32.93522,151.78164
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The core rising over the Tasman Sea above the Bogey Hole\
 , the ocean pool cut into the rock platform by convicts in about 1820.\nPr
 iority: Optional\n\nWHEN (Sydney time)\nNight of Fri 02 Apr into Sat 03 Ap
 r 2027.\nShoot window: 23:19 to 01:59 (core between 8° and 60° high\, sk
 y fully dark\, moon down\, low tide).\nRock platform shoot: the window is 
 cut to low tide plus or minus 90 minutes.\nBest composition: about 01:14\,
  core 30° high in the ESE.\nArrive by 22:34 to set up and focus.\nSunset 
 18:47 · astronomical dusk 20:09 · astronomical dawn 05:43 · sunrise 07:
 05\nMoon: new moon Wed 07 Apr 09:51. 19% lit and below the horizon during 
 the window. Moonrise Sat 03:13 · Moonset Fri 16:09\n\nCORE POSITION\n23:3
 0  altitude 10°\, azimuth 118° ESE\n00:00  altitude 16°\, azimuth 115°
  ESE\n00:30  altitude 22°\, azimuth 111° ESE\n01:00  altitude 28°\, azi
 muth 108° ESE\n01:30  altitude 34°\, azimuth 105° ESE\n02:00  altitude 
 40°\, azimuth 102° ESE\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\, Newcastle)\nNewcastle 
 is the nearest BOM standard port. Treat times as approximate for this site
 .\nThe window above is cut to low tide 00:30 (0.80 m) plus or minus 90 min
 utes.\nLow water Sat 00:30  0.80 m\nAt the best composition (01:14): about
  0.83 m and rising.\nPredictions exclude swell\, wind setup and wave run u
 p. Check BOM coastal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nSource table:
  https://www.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP004.pdf\n\nCAMERA
  POSITION\nThe Bogey Hole\, below King Edward Park\, York Drive\, Newcastl
 e NSW 2300\nCamera pin: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-3
 2.93522\,151.78164\nFace ESE (azimuth 107°) at 01:14.\nStraight line from
  Neutral Bay: about 113 km.\n\nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\nFE 12-
 24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm for single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II for a sh
 arper multi row panorama.\n12 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm: up t
 o 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 mm f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForeground: 
 separate longer frames at ISO 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from the s
 ame tripod position.\nPeak Design travel tripod\, red head torch\, dew hea
 ter strap on the lens.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Access: steps lead down from King
  Edward Park to the pool platform. Park on York Drive or at the top of The
  Terrace and walk down through the park.\n- Official listing: free entry. 
 Not suitable for people with access needs.\n- Waves break over the pool in
  any real swell\, and people have been washed off these rocks. Shoot from 
 the steps or the cliff top if sets reach the platform.\n- Open ocean to th
 e ESE. Newcastle city glow sits behind you to the west.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE Y
 OU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pin and time set): https://app.photoe
 phemeris.com/?ll=-32.93522\,151.78164&center=-32.93522\,151.78164&z=15&dt=
 2027-04-02T14%3A14%3A00.000Z\nPhotoPills: Planner > drop the pin at the ca
 mera coordinates > set the date and time above > Milky Way layer. Use Nigh
 t AR on site to confirm the core path.\nCheck cloud (BOM and Windy) and li
 ght pollution (lightpollutionmap.info) two days out.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phas
 es: US Naval Observatory 2027 table (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nSun\, moon and co
 re positions: computed with Skyfield and JPL DE421 for the camera pin.\nCo
 ordinates: OpenStreetMap. Terrain horizons: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.\nT
 ide predictions: Bureau of Meteorology 2027 tide tables\, Copyright Common
 wealth of Australia 2026. Based on Bureau of Meteorology information that 
